:''For the enemy encountered in the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]], see [[The 10th Angel (Enemy)|The 10th Angel]].''
'''The 10th Angel''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. It was added in [[Version 10.2 Update|Version 10.2]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 550
|rarity = UR
|name1 = The 10th Angel
|name2 = 10th Angel Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''10th Angel Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
The 10th Angel's extreme piercing range sounds impressive on paper, as it not only stands far enough to avoid many melee Angels but can also hit targets much further away, catching huge clusters of them at once, and its surge does increase its potency somewhat, dealing two additional hits if they connect for widespread devastation. This advantage is further amplified when it's close to the enemy base, as Omni Strike units stand at their maximum range.

However, despite its obvious strengths, The 10th Angel remains a lackluster unit with its several other weaknesses, starting with the general nature of Angels. Many of them are highly aggressive, short-ranged pushers, which can't be easily defeated by the unit's slow attack rate and low overall damage, surge included. More often than not, the surge will miss, and so does two thirds of its damage. Even the freeze duration is too short for it to matter when better options to stall melee angels exist. The few higher-ranged exceptions, such as [[Sunfish Jones|Jones]], are barely outranged by it, yet more efficient counters also exist for demolishing them. Its extreme cooldown and low health only hinder it further, as Angel pushers can very easily destroy everything in their way, with such stages often requiring a constant stream of replacements, so while it can stand far enough to avoid them, it really doesn't have other abilities to defend itself once they get too close.

{{Job|Classification = Sniper}}

